as mixed at', 0.9871060569235619], [[[197.00521850585938, 447.98388671875], [1499.674560546875, 445.7661437988281], [1499.674560546875, 481.25], [197.00521850585938, 483.4677429199219]], 'bedside or by the transport team, and administered in a similar fashion and for similar indications', 0.9936540283337988], [[[197.00521850585938, 485.68548583984375], [1437.6953125, 483.4677429199219], [1437.6953125, 520.0604858398438], [197.00521850585938, 522.2782592773438]], 'as routine surfactant therapy. The infants receiving budesonide had a median birth weight of', 0.9949802911799887], [[[198.1119842529297, 524.4959716796875], [1437.6953125, 522.2782592773438], [1437.6953125, 557.7620849609375], [198.1119842529297, 559.9798583984375]], '850g and gestational age of 26.7 weeks (Table 1). It was observed that BPD or death did not', 0.9935056652341571], [[[200.32553100585938, 562.1975708007812], [1472.0052490234375, 563.3064575195312], [1472.0052490234375, 596.5725708007812], [200.32553100585938, 595.4637451171875]], 'change between the historical surfactant cohort (71%, n=294) and the budesonide cohort (69%,', 0.9989681963039481], [[[200.32553100585938, 602.116943359375], [1497.4609375, 602.116943359375], [1497.4609375, 634.2742309570312], [200.32553100585938, 634.2742309570312]], 'n=173) (Table 2). However, budesonide was associated with a decrease in the need for continued', 0.9906986799645932], [[[197.00521850585938, 638.709716796875], [1489.713623046875, 637.600830078125], [1489.713623046875, 674.1935424804688], [197.00521850585938, 675.3024291992188]], 'mechanical ventilation, severe BPD type II or death (19% to 12%), grade II BPD or death (31%', 0.9883682948091755], [[[198.1119842529297, 679.7379150390625], [1401.171875, 677.5201416015625], [1401.171875, 709.6774291992188], [198.1119842529297, 711.8951416015625]], 'to 21%) (Table 2). Histologic chorioamnionitis was associated with decreased budesonide', 0.9897983855214613], [[[201.4322967529297, 717.4395141601562], [1480.859375, 717.4395141601562], [1480.859375, 750.7056274414062], [201.4322967529297, 750.7056274414062]], 'effects. Secondary morbidities (NEC, IVH, ROP, Sepsis) were similar (Table 3) and the median', 0.9926628243664036], [[[197.00521850585938, 755.14111328125], [1418.8802490234375, 752.9234008789062], [1418.8802490234375, 789.51611328125], [197.00521850585938, 791.73388671875]], 'gestational age at discharge was one week earlier (Table 4). This retrospective cohort study', 0.9941469774298046], [[[198.1119842529297, 793.9515991210938], [1436.588623046875, 791.73388671875], [1436.588623046875, 825.0], [198.1119842529297, 827.2177734375]], 'provides some reassuring data regarding short-term safety. As severe BPD was reduced with', 0.991889348190822], [[[200.32553100585938, 831.6532592773438], [1405.5989990234375, 831.6532592773438], [1405.5989990234375, 864.9193725585938], [200.32553100585938, 864.9193725585938]], 'budesonide, it is possible that there may be potential benefits due to reduction of postnatal', 0.9964276750882467], [[[198.1119842529297, 869.3548583984375], [1479.752685546875, 867.1370849609375], [1479.752685546875, 903.7298583984375], [198.1119842529297, 905.9475708007812]], 'steroid use, and lower rates of neurodevelopmental impairment (due to reduction in severe BPD', 0.984435369891505], [[[200.32553100585938, 909.2742309570312], [630.859375, 909.2742309570312], [630.859375, 942.5403442382812], [200.32553100585938, 942.5403442382812]], 'and in use of postnatal steroids).', 0.9874531346208909], [[[564.453125, 979.133056640625], [677.34375, 979.133056640625], [677.34375, 1010.1814575195312], [564.453125, 1010.1814575195312]], 'Table 1', 0.9872614996773856], [[[768.0989990234375, 980.241943359375], [1134.440185546875, 980.241943359375], [1134.440185546875, 1013.508056640625], [768.0989990234375, 1013.508056640625]], 'Demographicsof Cohorts', 0.9791176969354803], [[[1091.276123046875, 1020.1613159179688], [1272.7864990234375, 1020.1613159179688], [1272.7864